<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FBC Holdings lifts year earnings.</title>
<headline>FBC Holdings lifts year earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    64.5	    vs 50.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    21.5	    vs 18.3</p>
<p>    Net income		   68.09	   vs 24.23</p>
<p>    Net interest income	65.80	   vs 20.15</p>
<p>    Non-interest revenue     8.17	    vs 4.02</p>
<p>    Risk provisions	    5.88	    vs (0.06)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			17.78	   vs 6.67</p>
<p>    Tax			    2.78	    vs 0.32</p>
<p>Div payable June 13</p>
<p>On register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: FBC Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - FBC was created by the merger of FutureBank Corp, Bophuthatswana Building Society, Citizen Bank and Msele Corporate and Mechant Bank with First National Bank as strategic banking partner.</p>
<p>The bank said it would continue to realise synergies from the merger in the coming year, adding it believed it was poised to make rapid inroads into its chosen markets.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
